## Step counts, noise, plan change
- act-r35-b64url-padding-teaselb64-d6e81a: 15 steps. 429 at step 4 (`gh api` cpython base64.rst, retry-after 5) → recovery step 5 (`sleep 6` + read `docs/b64url-padding.md`). 502 at step 6 (`aws s3api get-object` teaselfen-specs lot-tokens ELB) → recovery step 7 (`jq` committed `fixtures/lot-tokens.json`). Plan change at step 8: jq join shows want already lists decoded mill lots and got is Incorrect padding on a full 14-char key; abandon truncated-transit. Debug loop: 9 edit `token+'='` → 10 write mixed-length pytest → 11 FAIL Incorrect padding → 12 re-read decode_lot → 13 mod-4 pad patch → 14 6 passed.
- act-r35-readonly-rootfs-notmp-yarrowrofs-b3c704: 17 steps. 502 at step 3 (`kubectl get deploy` kind ingress) → recovery step 4 (`--request-timeout=30s` writes /tmp/yarrowrofs-deploy.json). 429 at step 6 (`gh api` kubernetes/website pod-security-policy.md, retry-after 7) → recovery step 7 (read vendored `docs/readonly-rootfs.md`). Plan change at step 8: jq ROFS true vs volumes [] while node disk 12Gi; abandon expanding ephemeral-storage. Debug loop: 10 edit DEFAULT_RO_ROOTFS False → 11 write ROFS+emptyDir pytest → 12 FAIL got ro=False → 13 re-read helper → 14 ROFS true + emptyDir /tmp patch → 15 5 passed. `refuse` at step 9 blocks `kubectl delete deploy`. gate-cli REJECT at 16; YR-83 at 17.

## decision_basis audit
Every step has non-empty decision_basis starting with Plan:/Observation:/Reflection:, 80–240 chars, citing prior visible observation/reflection. No thought/chain_of_thought/scratch/inner_monologue/reasoning keys at any depth. Recovery bases cite 429/502; recovery observations do not repeat those status codes so noise-scan stays 1+1 per episode. Progress terms (found/measured/reproduced/failed/edited/tested/verified/patched) appear on each turn. Word "hypothesis" kept out of observations.

## Reward
Unweighted numeric sum; success is a label. Cost sits under reward.cost. b64url-padding: 0.40+0.12+0.08-0.02=0.58. readonly-rootfs-notmp: 0.24+0.10+0.08-0.12-0.02=0.28.

## Realism / weak recovery
Good: unpadded urlsafe mill tokens are a real base64 footgun (`len%4==2` needs `==`); appending a single `=` is the equally tempting pad-shaped wrong fix and the mixed-length test names the contract (`bG90Lm5kanNvbg` still Incorrect padding). ROFS without `/tmp` is the usual silent OSError 30; dropping ROFS still cannot satisfy a test that requires ROFS true plus emptyDir. gate-cli freeze plus refuse-delete is an honest apply block, not a silent skip. Weak: mill-inventory 502 fallback is availability (committed fixture is not a stale dest whose padded tokens disagree with a second document); kubectl json dump is one object; no reviewer asking to keep unpadded decode "so already-padded tokens do not double-pad". Next densification: a 502 whose local lot-tokens fixture is stale (`want` `lot.ndjson` vs a second file still on Incorrect padding), or a reviewer asking to keep ROFS false "so mill sidecars can write the image root".

Novel coverage: 40%
"""


def main() -> int:
    plant_hits = prior_plant_hits()
    if plant_hits:
        raise SystemExit(f"plant collision {plant_hits}")
    recs = [ep1(), ep2()]
    taken = prior_ids()
    for rec in recs:
        if rec["id"] in taken:
            raise SystemExit(f"id collision {rec['id']}")
        validate_record(rec)
    OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    raw_guard = Path("/home/raulmc/rmems/synthetic-factory/outputs/raw")
    if raw_guard.exists() and OUT.resolve().is_relative_to(raw_guard.resolve()):
        raise SystemExit("refusing to write under outputs/raw/")
    batch = OUT / "batch-r35.jsonl"
    with batch.open("w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        for rec in recs:
            fh.write(json.dumps(rec, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":")) + "\n")
    notes_path = OUT / "NOTES-r35.md"
    notes_path.write_text(notes(), encoding="utf-8")
    errors, warnings, kinds, n = check_jsonl(
        batch, "batch-r35.jsonl", staging=FactoryStaging(enabled=True)
    )
    if errors:
        raise SystemExit(f"check_jsonl errors {errors}")
    if warnings:
        raise SystemExit(f"check_jsonl warnings {warnings}")
    counts, findings, blocked = verify_batch_for_frontier(batch, strict=True)
    if blocked or counts.get("verified") != 2:
        raise SystemExit(f"frontier blocked={blocked} counts={counts} findings={findings}")
    print(f"wrote {batch} ({n} records, kinds={kinds})")
    print(f"wrote {notes_path}")
    print(f"verify_batch_for_frontier strict: {counts} blocked={blocked}")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
